  "derived_checks": [
    "Atomic adduct mass and electron removal/addition are evaluated directly from pinned constants. Hydrogen atomic mass differs slightly from PROTON+ELECTRON, so the proton-adduct mass shift is small but nonzero.",
    "Average-mass shifts retain the same monoisotopic proton/electron compensation. Sodium has one isotope with abundance 1 and equal average/monoisotopic mass; the class-test comment implying otherwise is not an asserted golden.",
    "Numeric-only fragments become empty after stoichiometric coefficient stripping and are defined no-ops. Formula-part minus signs split terms rather than becoming negative element counts.",
    "StringUtils toInt32 strips one leading plus and then accepts a negative integer, so a charge magnitude beginning +- is accepted before final-polarity normalization. Only space/tab/newline/carriage-return whitespace is stripped.",
    "Compatibility compares candidate counts against negated adduct counts, including signed counts and isotope identity; it ignores charge and molecular multiplier.",
    "All finite negative and zero scalar mass inputs retain source arithmetic. Checked nonfinite inputs/results, zero invariants, i32 minimum charge and native formula-count overflow are explicit safety boundaries."
  ],
